      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "@{64873f159cf028090ce2c2e2|full_name} Didn't see this until now, the avatar I tested initially is still broken. I also updated the SDK from the 3.6.2 beta to the 3.7.0 release but the issue hasn't changed.\n\nIt only uses 1 parent constraint on a gameobject that's parented under the head bone, so it shouldn't be the head bone tracking messing with it.\n\nI've uploaded the variant of the avatar to the ID avtr_75f8493b-b10b-4401-b659-6632b9798421\n\n(specifically this happens on Customization> Dullahan\n\nThe idea was to make the head shatter able in a quest paritable way)\n\nInterestingly animations like the landing animation can update the contact during the animation but that's the only information I have beyond the post, I haven't had the time to test more with contacts+constraints. And I haven't had anyone test it on quest for me either.",
